---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// The score (milestone 5): counted here, at build time, from the page
// sources themselves, so the numbers printed in the promise section are
// whatever the site actually contains on the day it is built. A page is
// a tool page when it imports one of the tool engines; the tool count
// is the number of distinct engines, so preset pages and translations
// count as pages, never as new tools. Nothing below is typed by hand.
const pageSources = import.meta.glob('./**/*.astro', { query: '?raw', eager: true, import: 'default' });
const TOOL_ENGINES = ['remove-bg', 'compress-pdf', 'compress-image', 'merge-pdf', 'split-pdf', 'ocr-pdf', 'size-checker', 'sign-pdf', 'flatten-pdf'];
// Runner scripts (milestone 6): pages that work files through the
// engines above (batch doors, interleave, workflow chains) are tool
// pages, but they are not new tools, so they never add to the tool
// count. The audit in verify/seo-audit.mjs holds the same two lists;
// keep them identical.
const PAGE_SCRIPTS = ['batch-pdf', 'batch-image', 'batch-remove-bg', 'workflows', 'interleave-pdf'];
const enginesUsed = new Set();
let toolPages = 0;
for (const src of Object.values(pageSources)) {
  const found = TOOL_ENGINES.filter((e) => src.includes(`scripts/${e}.js`));
  const runner = PAGE_SCRIPTS.some((e) => src.includes(`scripts/${e}.js`));
  if (found.length || runner) {
    toolPages++;
    found.forEach((e) => enginesUsed.add(e));
  }
}
// (+1: a glob never returns the importing file itself, so this page
// adds itself back. Verified against the built page count, 26.)
const pageCount = Object.keys(pageSources).length + 1;
const toolCount = enginesUsed.size;

const nevers = [
  ['No accounts', 'The tools need no account, no sign-up and no card. There is nothing to cancel because there is nothing to join.'],
  ['No daily counters', 'There is no counter in any tool. Nothing counts your jobs, so nothing can run out. Do a job twice, or two hundred times; the page does not keep score.'],
  ['No credits, no minutes, no meters', 'No unit of work is sold here. The price of a job is known before you start: free.'],
  ['No watermarks', 'Your output is yours. Nothing of ours is stamped, printed or hidden on it.'],
  ['No download held for payment', 'The download button is the end of the job, never the start of a checkout. On other sites the price often appears at that exact click; here it is just a download.'],
  ['No fake buttons', 'Every button on a tool page does the thing its label says. Nothing here is dressed up to look like a download and act like an advert.'],
  ['No smaller free size', 'Output is made at your file\'s own size. There is no small free tier and no big paid tier, because there are no tiers.'],
  ['No upload', 'Your files are processed in your browser and are never sent to us. There is no server here that could receive them.'],
];
---

<Base title="What free means here · Benchzy" description="The never list, in plain words: no accounts, no counters, no credits, no watermarks, no download held for payment. Why it can be true, and the one real limit, your device.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">Standing page · the commitment</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">What free means here</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        "Free" is the most abused word in file tools. It usually means a ration: a few jobs a
        day, a small output, a download that turns into a checkout. This page is the written
        commitment for what the word means on Benchzy, so the promise can be checked, not just
        believed. This is a public commitment, in writing, here; if it ever changed, this page
        would have to change first, in public.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
      {nevers.map(([title, body]) => (
        <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">{title}</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">The aim, stated as a promise</p>
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold mt-2">One workshop, every job</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Our promise: every file job in one place. We are growing Benchzy into the biggest toolkit
        on the web, tool by tool, and the count below is the score.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-5 max-w-md">
        <div class="spec-row"><dt>working tools</dt><dd>{toolCount}</dd></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><dt>tool pages</dt><dd>{toolPages}</dd></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><dt>pages in all</dt><dd>{pageCount}</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Counted by the build from the site itself, on the day this page was built. "Biggest" is
        the aim on this page, not a claim about today; the growth is the point, and every tool
        that ships moves the score. The tools themselves are listed on the
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-deep" href="/tools/">all tools page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Why it can be free</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The big sites charge because every job runs on their computers and costs them money,
          so the job has to be rationed. Benchzy's tools run inside your web browser, on your
          device. A job here costs this site nothing, so there is nothing to ration. Premium is
          free here because the work runs on your computer, not ours. The site itself is paid
          for by ads on the pages; an ad can see which page you are on, and can never see your
          file, because your file never leaves the page's memory.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">The one real limit</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The limit is your device, not us. We set no limit on jobs or file counts. Your browser
          and device set the real ones: very large files can run out of memory, and a small
          phone is slower than a desktop. When a job cannot run on your device, the tool says so
          in plain words before or as it starts, and your file is unchanged. A second limit is
          honest too: pages and programs you have used are saved by your browser, so those
          tools can open again without a connection; a tool you have never opened still needs
          one first visit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-10 p-6 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Do not take our word for it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft max-w-2xl">
        The no-upload promise can be watched, live, while a job runs:
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/check-it-yourself/">check it yourself</a>.
        The engines behind every tool, and their licences, are named on the
        <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/credits/">credits page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
